                         DD-Request V1.1 by Hydra

  Introduction + Features
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

  This door allows users to leave requests to other users. It's kinda
  powerful and has some features like:

   - Generates datafile of requests.
   - User interface is lightbar driven, so cursor keys are supported.
   - Generates a message about request. (Optional)
   - Message outlook is 100% SysOp configurable.
   - Requests can be deleted by requester of SysOp.
   - Coded in C.
   - Source code included.

   Installation
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~

   Install this as a normal DayDream Door. Place the configfile in the
   directory where you keep your configfiles usually.

   Add something like this to DayDream.CFG:

DOOR_COMMAND.. REQ
DOOR_TYPE..... 1
DOOR_SECURITY. 5
DOOR_EXECUTE.. Doors:Request %N

   Check out the configfile about configuration information.

   You may edit message the message outlook by changing the message design
   file (Check out the configfile!).

   following control codes are available in message design file:

   %r = Request
   %a = Author
   %d = Date


